        "seo_questions": {
          "bn": "",
          "de": "",
          "en": "According to Imam al-Sadiq (AS), do believers suffer when divine punishment descends upon a sinful people?",
          "es": "",
          "fa": "",
          "fr": "",
          "id": "",
          "ru": "",
          "tr": "",
          "ur": "",
          "zh": ""
        },
        "summaries": {
          "bn": "",
          "de": "",
          "en": "This hadith from Imam Abu Abdullah al-Sadiq (AS) addresses whether divine punishment sent upon a people also strikes the believers present among them. The Imam (AS) affirms that believers are indeed struck by such collective punishment, but crucially distinguishes their fate: they are ultimately delivered and saved after it, unlike those upon whom the punishment is truly deserved. This teaching illuminates the Shia theological understanding that worldly tribulation is not necessarily a sign of divine wrath against the believer, and that divine protection (wilayah) ensures their ultimate salvation.",
          "es": "",
          "fa": "",
          "fr": "",
          "id": "",
          "ru": "",
          "tr": "",
          "ur": "",
          "zh": ""
        },
